### Panda Pocket - Rate service
###
### Executable from Rider and from the VS Code REST Client extension.
### These requests are kept in the repository deliberately: they are
### version-controlled examples that double as API documentation and cannot
### drift away from the code the way an exported Postman collection can.
###
### The service is published on 5003. Once the gateway exists (day 3) the same
### calls route through http://localhost:5000.

@rate = http://localhost:5003

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health. Probes MongoDB rather than merely confirming the process is alive,
### so it reports Unhealthy with a 503 when the database is unreachable.
### Try it: docker compose stop mongo, then call this again.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/health

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Current rate for every configured pair. Served from memory, not MongoDB.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/api/rates

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### One pair. This is the call the Invoice service makes on the critical path
### when creating an invoice, and the call that gets a circuit breaker in front
### of it on day 6.
###
### The asOf field matters: when the breaker is open and Invoice falls back to a
### cached rate, asOf is how it knows and reports how stale that rate is.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/BTCZAR

###
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/ETHZAR

### USDTZAR is configured with near-zero volatility because it is a stablecoin.
### Call it repeatedly and it barely moves, while BTCZAR wanders. That is a
### configured property of each pair, not one blanket simulation.
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/USDTZAR

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Unknown pair returns 404, not a zero rate. Returning zero would let Invoice
### compute an infinite crypto amount from a typo in an asset name, which is
### exactly the kind of failure that should be loud rather than silent.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/DOGEZAR

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Tick history, served from MongoDB. Newest first. Defaults to the last hour
### when no range is supplied, and is capped at 5000 points regardless of the
### window asked for, so a careless request cannot pull the whole collection.
###
### This read is "one pair, newest first, within a time range", which is exactly
### a prefix match on the compound index { pair: 1, ts: -1 } followed by an
### ordered range scan. Mongo satisfies both the filter and the sort from the
### index, with no in-memory sort stage.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/BTCZAR/history

### An explicit window. Points from the startup backfill carry
### source "gbm-backfill"; live ones carry "gbm-simulator". The two form one
### continuous series rather than meeting at a visible seam.
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/BTCZAR/history?from=2026-08-24T00:00:00Z&to=2026-08-26T00:00:00Z

### An inverted range returns 400 rather than an empty list, because silently
### returning nothing hides a caller's bug.
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/BTCZAR/history?from=2026-08-25T10:00:00Z&to=2026-08-25T09:00:00Z

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Correlation id. Supply one and it is echoed on the response and stamped on
### every log line the request produces. Filter Seq by it at
### http://localhost:5341 to see the request summary with its status code and
### elapsed time. From day 3 onwards the same id spans several services.
###
### Omit the header and the service mints one, so a request made directly from
### this file still produces traceable logs instead of a gap.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/api/rates/BTCZAR
X-Correlation-Id: manual-trace-001

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### OpenAPI document. Swagger UI is at {{rate}}/swagger and is deliberately
### enabled outside development, because a running container that produces its
### own specification is better evidence than a JSON file committed by hand.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{rate}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
